firedamp
========

Methane plume aggregator. Maps satellite-detected methane plumes
alongside candidate O&G infrastructure sources, and shows a per-plume
source attribution produced offline by a research agent (the ch4id
sibling repo) and served from a static dataset.

Live: https://research.datadesk.eco/firedamp/


Plume sources
-------------
- Carbon Mapper      satellite + aircraft hyperspectral (API)
- IMEO / MARS        UNEP methane plume database (Azure zip)
- SRON               TROPOMI weekly plume CSVs (FTP)
- ch4id catalogue    OGIM + OSM + MapStand + GEM candidate sources


Repo layout
-----------
A cartograph app (github.com/data-desk-eco/cartograph — the map
system itself is documented there), vendored, with all firedamp
behaviour in three app modules.

    web/             static frontend (ES modules)
      config.js        declarative cartograph config: sources, layers,
                       filters, key, data table, detail panel
      attribution.js   attribution lookup/render + wind stat
      candidates.js    candidate infrastructure from the ch4id
                       catalogue (FlatGeobuf bbox queries over GCS)
      style.css
      index.html
      data/            plumes.parquet (built), attributions.parquet
                       (committed source of truth, from ch4id)
      vendor/          cartograph core, dd design dist, MapLibre,
                       hyparquet, FlatGeobuf, Inter font
    scripts/         Python ETL (uv-managed) + build/deploy shell
      fetch_carbon_mapper.py
      fetch_imeo.py
      fetch_sron.py
      build.py         source CSVs -> web/data/plumes.parquet
      features.sql     ch4id catalogue -> web/data/features.fgb
      dist.sh          assembles the Pages artifact (cache-busted)
      serve.py         dev server with HTTP Range for FlatGeobuf
      vendor.sh
    data/            input CSVs and intermediates (gitignored)
    .github/workflows/
      deploy.yml          Pages on push to main
      update-data.yml     plume refresh every 6 h


Setup
-----
Requires Python (managed with uv); the feature catalogue rebuild
additionally requires duckdb.

    make vendor        vendor JS/CSS/fonts (cartograph, dd, ...)
    make serve         dev server on :8000


Pipelines
---------
    make data             fetch CM + SRON + IMEO, build plumes.parquet
    make features         ch4id catalogue -> features.fgb
    make features-upload  upload features.fgb to GCS
    make rebuild          full pipeline: data + features + upload


Source attribution
------------------
Detail panels show a per-plume source attribution, produced offline
by the ch4id sibling repo's agentic pipeline (make deploy there
commits a refreshed web/data/attributions.parquet here and pushes).
The parquet is the committed source of truth and is read directly in
the browser, as is plumes.parquet. There is no live
in-browser LLM pipeline. See CLAUDE.md.


URL scheme
----------
    Map position     #map=<zoom>/<lat>/<lon>
    Plume permalink  #plume=<id>


Deployment
----------
Push to main -> deploy.yml -> GitHub Pages. All data is served live
from the central datadesk store (the CloudFerro bucket
https://s3.WAW3-2.cloudferro.com/datadesk-archive): update-data.yml
rebuilds plumes/data.parquet there every 6 h, and the ch4id repo
publishes the feature catalogue to features/data.fgb
(range-requested).

`make deploy-private` ships a Cloudflare Pages build (behind
Cloudflare Access) that additionally includes the local-only GHGSat
data and Data Desk's own detections (`make dd` — MARS-S2L / hypergas
candidates from the store, pending analyst review) — the only deploy
that ever contains either.

Both workflows assemble the Pages artifact via scripts/dist.sh — add
any new web asset there.


